In article <19925.4188.9499@dosgate> michael.kitts@canrem.com (michael kitts) writes:

    1) After offering some corpes at my alter, I recieved two weapons. One
   is  +0 Long Sword named Giant Slayer, and the other is +0 Long Sword
   named Frost Brand. Which would be the better weapon, I am on dungeon
   level 7 and I am playing a Wizard.
      (*first I have to get rid of the cursed -1 scimitar that is stuck to
   my hand!!)

Frost Brand is generally considered the best weapon in the game, and
it's certainly better than Giant Slayer. (The only alternatives to
Frost Brand are Stormbringer and Excalibur. I prefer Excalibur because
it's the easiest to get. You get it early in almost any game and then
you don't think of the weapons problem anymore. Also, if you make it
yourself, Excalibur is rustproof, which saves a scroll to better use.)

     2) I tried to sit on a throne and was happily reward with a prompt
   asking which nasty I wished genocided! I was wondering what other events
   can occur from sitting on a throne?

A lot of things (10+ different, perhaps). Unfortunately, I don't have
the spoilers handy, but basically anything can happen. (You get a
wish, you gain ability, you get self-knowledgeable, you get un-cursed
and so on...) But beware! A lot of bad things may also happen. This is
somewhat dependent of your luck, so it may be a good idea to save
those thrones untli you know your luck is very hig.

     3) Finally, I am somehow invisible, I don't have a ring of
   invisibilty, but must have eaten something to make me invis. Is there a
   way to get RID of it?? I want to enter some more stores but  I'm not
   allowed in. How can I become un-invisible.

You can't. (Well, gremlins may steal an intrinsic randomly, but they
will probably kill you ten times over and take any other intrinsic you
may have before you lose that invisibility, so don't try this at home,
kids!) But then again, why would you want to lose it. It's one of the
best intrinsics, and there are ways to enter stores invisible.


